quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  12,70,"So when he had furnished them with their provisions, he placed the (king’s) drinking cup in his brother’s saddlebag. Then a herald called out: ‘O you men of the caravan! You are surely thieves.’"
  12,71,They turned towards them and said: ‘What are you missing?’
  12,72,They (the officials of the king’s court) said: ‘We are missing the king’s goblet. Whoever brings it shall have a camel load (of corn).’ (The steward said:) ‘I shall be its guarantor.’
  12,73,"They said: ‘By Allah! You certainly know that we did not come to cause corruption in the land, and we are not thieves.’"
  12,74,They (the officials of the king’s court) said: ‘What shall be its penalty if you are lying?’
  12,75,"They said: ‘Its penalty will be that in whoever’s saddlebag it is found, he shall give himself as its requital. That is how We punish the wrongdoers.’"
  12,76,"Then he (Yusuf) began with their bags before (opening) his brother’s bag. Then he took that (goblet) out of his brother’s bag. In this way, We devised a plan for Yusuf. He could not have held his brother under the king’s law unless Allah had so willed. We elevate in degrees whomever We please. And above every man of knowledge is one who knows better.*"
  12,77,"They said: ‘If he has stolen, (it comes as no surprise as) his full brother has also stolen before.’ So Yusuf (Joseph) kept his secret hidden in his heart and did not disclose it to them. He said (in his heart): ‘You are (still) in a worse state. And Allah knows best what you allege.’"
  12,78,"They said: ‘Respectable governor! Indeed, he has a venerable, aged father. Could you take one of us in his place? Indeed, we see you are a gracious person.’"
